    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** anchoring the lineup as the clear objective starts. **Gunnar Henderson** carries an elite 83.29 score, benefiting immensely from a plus-matchup against a vulnerable 4.35 xERA arm in Peralta and a distinct advantage in our \"Slow SP Delivery\" metric, which enhances his stolen base probability. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (74.88) and **Andy Pages** (74.11) are prioritized against Bubba Chandler; their scores are bolstered significantly by the pitcher's high xERA and favorable game environment. While **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** are currently pending official lineup confirmation, their projected spots in the batting order provide the requisite leverage to remain locked into the starting nine.\n\nOutside of the top tier, **Nasim Nunez** (51.84) stands out as an intriguing play; while his raw base is moderate, the 88% stolen base opportunity against Gusto\u2019s delivery speed makes him a critical asset for our 5x5 needs. Conversely, **Luis Robert Jr.** presents the most volatility today. Despite a decent base projection, his score sits at a marginal 41.50, suppressed by a difficult matchup against Burke and a 37% rain risk. He narrowly avoids the bench, as we continue to hunt for speed, but he remains a candidate for mid-game defensive substitution if the weather worsens. \n\nThe decision to bench **Dominic Smith** (37.94) was the most difficult, as he hovered just below our 40.0 floor threshold. Ultimately, his matchup against Misiorowski\u2014a pitcher with a stifling 2.09 xERA\u2014rendered the platoon advantage negligible compared to the offensive upside of **Tommy White** (49.54) in the utility spot. We are also monitoring **Miguel Vargas** closely, as his respectable 49.18 score is compromised by the same 37% rain risk impacting **Luis Robert Jr.**. With **Jordan Westburg** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** confirmed on the IL, our depth is being tested, making it imperative that **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill** provide efficient production against their respective left-handed opponents to maintain our standing.",
